        "Key points of sine and cosine":"Over one period, `y = sin x` is on its axis going up at 0, at its maximum at π/2, on its axis going down at π, at its minimum at 3π/2, and back on its axis at 2π. `y = cos x` is at its maximum at 0, on its axis going down at π/2, at its minimum at π, on its axis going up at 3π/2, and at its maximum again at 2π. The key points are a quarter period apart.",
