    blocks:[{ title:"Reading a wave, in four steps", html:"<ol><li><strong>Axis:</strong> `c` = (max + min) ÷ 2.</li><li><strong>Amplitude:</strong> `|a|` = (max − min) ÷ 2.</li><li><strong>Period:</strong> the distance between neighbouring maximums, or twice the distance from a maximum to the next minimum. Then `k` = 2π ÷ period.</li><li><strong>Start:</strong> choose a form and find its starting point: cos at a maximum, sin on the axis going up, −cos at a minimum, −sin on the axis going down. `d` is that point’s `x`-coordinate. A start one period earlier or later works just as well.</li></ol>" }]
